3. (1) There shall be a Parliamentary Service Council which shall
have the responsibility for matters relating to the Parliamentary
Service.
 (2) The Parliamentary Service Council shall consist of the
following members:
 (a) the President of the Senate as a Chairman;
 (b) the Speaker of the House of Representatives as
a Co-Chairman;
 (c) the Deputy President of the Senate;
 (d) two Deputy Speakers of the House of Representatives;
 (e) two members of the Senate who are nominated by
the Committee of Selection of the Senate and approved
by a resolution of the Senate;
 (f) four members of the House of Representatives of which
two are members of the Government and two are members
of the group in Opposition, who are nominated by
the Committee of Selection of the House of Representatives
and approved by a resolution of the House of Representatives;
 (g) the Clerk to the Senate;
 (h) the Clerk to the House of Representatives;
Parliamentary Service
 (i) the Secretary General of Treasury or his representative
as an ex-officio  member;
 (j) the Director General of Public Service or his representative
as an ex-officio  member; and
 (k) the Chief Administrator of Parliament as an ex-officio
member.
